===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|ang|sv}} {{term|cross|lang=ang}}, {{etyl|sga|sv}} {{term|cross|lang=sga}} or {{etyl|fro|sv}} {{term|crois|lang=fro}} < {{etyl|la|sv}} {{term|crux|lang=la}}. See ''[[cross]]''.

====Pronunciation====
* {{audio|Sv-kors.ogg|audio}}

====Noun====
{{sv-noun-n-zero|genitive=}}
{{infl|sv|noun|g=n}}

# [[cross]]; a geometrical figure consisting of one horizontal line, and an intersecting vertical line such that at least one of them is divided in half by the other.
# {{heraldry|lang=sv}} geometrical figures similar to a cross as in definition 1.
# A wooden post with a perpendicular beam attached and used (e.g. in the Roman Empire) to execute criminals (i.e. by crucifixion).
# [[dagger]] (†); a text character

